From e58ba367ad59880cf392a64415a61447d2894a31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:01:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-qcom: kaanapali MDSS keeps the bootloader's
 scanout

The bootloader leaves the display fetching its splash. In a translated
domain every fetch faulted from the SMMU probe on, and the panel showed
black until msm took over, about 1.8 s. Like the other MDSS blocks, it
now starts in an identity domain until msm attaches its own.
---
 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
index 795e8ec7e8fa..0ee9a9cfdf8e 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/arm-smmu-qcom.c
@@ -407,6 +407,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_smmu_client_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,adreno" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,adreno-gmu" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-mdss" },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,kaanapali-mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdp4" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,mdss" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,qcm2290-mdss" },
-- 
2.56.0

